From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom: use terminate fault policy for MSM8226 MDP

Match the MSM8226 BSP non-secure context fault model: its reset and
context-programming sequence does not set SCTLR.CFCFG. Terminate faults
instead of leaving a transaction pending after firmware-display handoff.
Keep fault interrupts and reporting enabled.

With the BFB table corrected, the native MDP still gives a100ms ATOS
translation timeout followed by recurrent vblank timeouts. This change
isolates stall policy; it does not change PHY, pixel clocks or page tables.
Physical LCD output and hardware translation must still be tested.

Link: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226/blob/3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256/drivers/iommu/msm_iommu-v1.c

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index 190de5957..4759f9798 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -1033,6 +1033,7 @@ static const struct qcom_iommu_bfb_reg msm8226_mdp_bfb[] = {
 };
 
 static const struct qcom_iommu_cfg msm8226_mdp_cfg = {
+	.no_stall = true,
 	.bfb = msm8226_mdp_bfb,
 	.num_bfb = ARRAY_SIZE(msm8226_mdp_bfb),
 };
